sts never show ",[315,1082,1083],{},"null",[275,1085,1087],{"id":1086},"documentation-site","Documentation site",[262,1089,1090,1091,1094,1095,1098,1099,1102,1103,1106,1107,1110,1111,1114,1115,1118,1119,1122,1123,1126,1127,1130,1131,1134,1135,644],{},"The site is a standalone Nuxt app in ",[315,1092,1093],{},"docs\u002F"," (Nuxt 4, Nuxt UI, Nuxt Content; own ",[315,1096,1097],{},"pnpm-lock.yaml",", not a root workspace package). Pages live in ",[315,1100,1101],{},"docs\u002Fcontent\u002F"," (numeric prefixes only order the sidebar). JS reference, Tauri commands, permissions and changelog pages are written by ",[315,1104,1105],{},"docs\u002Fscripts\u002Fgenerate.mjs"," on every build. Diagrams: edit ",[315,1108,1109],{},"docs\u002Fdiagrams\u002F*.mmd",", then ",[315,1112,1113],{},"pnpm -C docs diagrams"," re-renders the committed SVGs in ",[315,1116,1117],{},"docs\u002Fpublic\u002Fdiagrams\u002F"," (needs Chrome). Illustrations: ",[315,1120,1121],{},"docs\u002Fpublic\u002Fillustrations\u002F\u003Cname>.light.svg"," come from fal (",[315,1124,1125],{},"node docs\u002Fscripts\u002Fillustrations.mjs --generate \u003Cname>",", prompts in that script); the script writes the ",[315,1128,1129],{},".dark.svg"," twin by recoloring. Maintainer tooling is ",[315,1132,1133],{},"@tauri-plugin-widgets\u002Fscripts"," (citty + TypeScript under ",[315,1136,1137],{},"scripts\u002Fsrc",[262,1139,1140,1143,1144,518,1147,518,1150,1153,1154,1157,1158,1161,1162,313,1165,518,1168,1171,1172,1177,1178,432],{},[266,1141,1142],{},"Boundary:"," consumer commands (",[315,1145,1146],{},"preview",[315,1148,1149],{},"signing",[315,1151,1152],{},"doctor",", …) live in ",[315,1155,1156],{},"src-cli\u002F"," → published ",[315,1159,1160],{},"dist-cli\u002Fcli.mjs",". Visual stands \u002F goldens \u002F docs codegen live under ",[315,1163,1164],{},"scripts\u002F",[315,1166,1167],{},"pnpm hosts",[315,1169,1170],{},"pnpm cli:test","). See root ",[271,1173,1176],{"href":1174,"rel":1175},"https:\u002F\u002